    <string name="about_title">How to Use CBC Toolkit</string>
    <string name="about_subtitle">The best app for teachers following the Ugandan CBC Curriculum.</string>
    <string name="about_description">The CBC Teachers Toolkit is designed to empower Ugandan teachers with offline-first tools for effective classroom delivery. It streamlines the transition to the New Lower Secondary Curriculum.</string>
    <string name="how_to_use_title">Key Functions &amp; Guide</string>
    <string name="how_to_use_1">1. <b>Browse &amp; Search:</b> Access a complete database of S1-S4 topics, lesson plans, and teaching tips.</string>
    <string name="how_to_use_2">2. <b>Scheme Builder:</b> Create A4 landscape Schemes of Work. Save them offline or share as PDF.</string>
    <string name="how_to_use_3">3. <b>My Library:</b> Save your favorite topics and add personal teaching observations as notes.</string>
    <string name="how_to_use_4">4. <b>Offline Resources:</b> Download NCDC guides and videos to use them in the classroom without internet.</string>
    <string name="how_to_use_5">5. <b>Accessibility:</b> Use the \'Read Aloud\' feature to listen to lesson content while multi-tasking.</string>
